{
  "case_id": "2001-01-419",
  "document_hash": "60ce850b398a2b65470859920ab0e204e16834a6e2d02fe3b203dcdba11a9400",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2001-01-419",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60ce850b398a2b65470859920ab0e204e16834a6e2d02fe3b203dcdba11a9400",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60ce850b398a-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SUTTON: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice. May it please the Court: The question presented in this case is whether Congress in 1994 divested the States of their traditional authority to delegate police powers over local safety matters to their political subdivisions. It would be no small matter for Congress to impose such a restriction on the States, and we submit they did no such thing in this instance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2001-01-419",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60ce850b398a2b65470859920ab0e204e16834a6e2d02fe3b203dcdba11a9400",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60ce850b398a-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, I think the argument on the other side, Mr. Sutton, is that the first section (a)(1) does say, no State or political subdivision thereof and no interstate agency. It talks about a political subdivision so that when you come down to the section you've just quoted, and it only says State, there's perhaps a fair inference that only a State and not a political subdivision is included."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Rehnquist",
      "case_id": "2001-01-419",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60ce850b398a2b65470859920ab0e204e16834a6e2d02fe3b203dcdba11a9400",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60ce850b398a-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: -- in which it says, shall not restrict the safety regulatory authority of a State. And you say that includes, you know, political subdivisions of a State.\nMR. SUTTON: No. That it includes the right to delegate political subdivisions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-419",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60ce850b398a2b65470859920ab0e204e16834a6e2d02fe3b203dcdba11a9400",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60ce850b398a-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Has there been any -- what's the closest case respondents could cite to show a contrary practice?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stewart",
      "case_id": "2001-01-419",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60ce850b398a2b65470859920ab0e204e16834a6e2d02fe3b203dcdba11a9400",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60ce850b398a-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. STEWART: We cited the Lee Deadwood case in our brief as support for the proposition that Congress would constitutionally be authorized to preempt municipal law without preempting State law if it chose."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cordray",
      "case_id": "2001-01-419",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60ce850b398a2b65470859920ab0e204e16834a6e2d02fe3b203dcdba11a9400",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60ce850b398a-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CORDRAY: The practical effect of the decision below, as you uncovered it in your questioning earlier, is that Federal law preempts municipalities and other local governments from imposing their own individual licensing schemes upon motor carriers of property and that is --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-419",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "60ce850b398a2b65470859920ab0e204e16834a6e2d02fe3b203dcdba11a9400",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60ce850b398a-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: It's not the best statute, is it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cordray",
      "case_id": "2001-01-419",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "60ce850b398a2b65470859920ab0e204e16834a6e2d02fe3b203dcdba11a9400",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60ce850b398a-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CORDRAY: It's -- it's clear enough with respect to the things we care about here, which is that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-419",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "60ce850b398a2b65470859920ab0e204e16834a6e2d02fe3b203dcdba11a9400",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60ce850b398a-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: No, but (c)(1) uses may enact or enforce just as -- as (c)(2)(C) does, whereas (c)(2)(A) does not. The to enact or enforce language applies in every subsection except the one that we're arguing about."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cordray",
      "case_id": "2001-01-419",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "60ce850b398a2b65470859920ab0e204e16834a6e2d02fe3b203dcdba11a9400",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60ce850b398a-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CORDRAY: That was my point. I was trying to make it earlier. I -- I didn't make it as clearly as you just did. But that's exactly --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Cordray",
      "case_id": "2001-01-419",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60ce850b398a2b65470859920ab0e204e16834a6e2d02fe3b203dcdba11a9400",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60ce850b398a-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CORDRAY: No. There's no substantive Tenth Amendment issue here. There's no commandeering of States or local governments to enact some sort of program. This is the same as the Court in Wolens where they said this statute must be read to say the State cannot legislate in this area, but they can enforce contracts through their courts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2001-01-419",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60ce850b398a2b65470859920ab0e204e16834a6e2d02fe3b203dcdba11a9400",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60ce850b398a-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Let's -- let's say we -- we disagree with that. Is -- is that not -- let's say we find the statute in -- in equipoise, or the arguments. Should we not give force to the argument petitioner makes that the States should be presumed to have the authority to determine how best to govern themselves?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Sutton",
      "case_id": "2001-01-419",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60ce850b398a2b65470859920ab0e204e16834a6e2d02fe3b203dcdba11a9400",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60ce850b398a-0003-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, the practical consequences -- I want to go back to again -- of their interpretation. (c)(2)(A), they've agreed, has to be construed the same way throughout, and there are countless -- as we indicated in our opening brief, every State in the country has delegations to cities that have size and weight controls, size and weight rules that would be eliminated by this particular construction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2001-01-419",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60ce850b398a2b65470859920ab0e204e16834a6e2d02fe3b203dcdba11a9400",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60ce850b398a-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
